@startuml runtime_topology
'
' Class diagram — orchestration, fleet, callbacks, and monitor_lock
' layers, after the per-job → singleton fleet monitor port.
'
' Reflects current state on the orchestration branch.
'

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title Runtime layer topology — orchestration / callbacks / fleets / monitor_lock

' ============================================================
' Orchestration layer
' ============================================================

package "orchestrator" #FFDDDD {
  class RenderOrchestrator <<facade>> {
    + on_job_succeeded(id)
    + on_job_failed(id, err)
    + on_job_running(id)
    + cancel_one_job(id)
    + is_job_terminal(id)
    + get_job_raw(id)
    + get_group_status(id)
  }
  class RenderLifecycle <<workhorse>> {
    + handle_chunk_succeeded(id)
    + handle_chunk_failed(id, err)
    + handle_chunk_running(id)
    + reconcile_group_status(gid)
    + cancel_one_job(id)
  }

  RenderOrchestrator --> RenderLifecycle : delegates
}

' ============================================================
' Callbacks layer (adapter between fleet outcomes and orchestrator)
' ============================================================

package "callbacks" #FFEEDD {
  class CallbackRouter <<funnel>> {
    + route(id, outcome, error?)
  }
  class SuccessHandler
  class FailureHandler

  CallbackRouter --> SuccessHandler : SUCCESS
  CallbackRouter --> FailureHandler : FAILURE
}

SuccessHandler --> RenderOrchestrator : on_job_succeeded
FailureHandler --> RenderOrchestrator : on_job_failed

' ============================================================
' Fleet layer
' ============================================================

package "fleets" #FFE4FF {
  class FleetRegistry {
    + register(strategy)
    + get(fleet_name)
  }

  package "strategies" {
    interface IFleetStrategy {
      + dispatch(task, ctx, job_id)
      + cancel(provider_job_id)
    }
    class VastFleetStrategy
    class ModalFleetStrategy
    class CommunityStrategy
    VastFleetStrategy ..|> IFleetStrategy
    ModalFleetStrategy ..|> IFleetStrategy
    CommunityStrategy ..|> IFleetStrategy
  }

  package "clients" {
    class VastClient {
      + dispatch_job()
      + cancel_job(id)
      + instances.list()
    }
    class ModalClient {
      + dispatch_job()
      + cancel_job(id)
    }
  }

  package "fleet monitors" #DDFFDD {
    class VastFleetMonitor <<singleton, 1 thread>> {
      + try_start()
      - _tick()
      - _inspect(row, inst)
    }
    class ModalFleetMonitor <<singleton, 1 thread>> {
      + try_start()
      - _tick()
      - _inspect(row)
    }
    class CommunityMonitor <<singleton, 1 thread>> {
      + try_start()
      - _tick()
    }
  }

  FleetRegistry o-- VastFleetStrategy
  FleetRegistry o-- ModalFleetStrategy
  FleetRegistry o-- CommunityStrategy
  VastFleetStrategy --> VastClient
  ModalFleetStrategy --> ModalClient
  VastFleetMonitor --> VastClient : list() once per tick\n+ destroy() on terminal
  ModalFleetMonitor --> ModalClient : cancel_job() on terminal
}

' ============================================================
' monitor_lock layer (the sweep daemon — name is a misnomer)
' ============================================================

package "monitor_lock" #DDEEFF {
  class MonitorLockFacade <<entry point>> {
    + start()
    + stop()
  }
  class MonitorLockSweeper <<every 30s tick>> {
    + start()
    + stop()
  }
  class MonitorLockRepository <<Redis lock primitive>> {
    + try_acquire(key, owner)
    + refresh(key, owner)
    + release(key, owner)
  }

  package "sweep strategies" {
    class MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy
    class MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy
    class MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy
    class MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy <<NEW>>
  }

  MonitorLockFacade --> MonitorLockSweeper
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy
  MonitorLockSweeper --> MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy
}

' ============================================================
' Cross-layer wiring
' ============================================================

' sweep strategies poke the singletons / lifecycle every tick
MonitorLockVastSweepStrategy --> VastFleetMonitor : try_start()
MonitorLockModalSweepStrategy --> ModalFleetMonitor : try_start()
MonitorLockCommunitySweepStrategy --> CommunityMonitor : try_start()
MonitorLockGroupAuditSweepStrategy --> RenderLifecycle : reconcile_group_status()

' singletons hold their per-fleet Redis lock through the lock repo
VastFleetMonitor ..> MonitorLockRepository : monitor:vast
ModalFleetMonitor ..> MonitorLockRepository : monitor:modal
CommunityMonitor ..> MonitorLockRepository : monitor:community

' singletons emit outcomes back up through the callback router
VastFleetMonitor ..> CallbackRouter : on_failure / on_success / on_running
ModalFleetMonitor ..> CallbackRouter : on_failure / on_success
CommunityMonitor ..> CallbackRouter : on_failure

' lifecycle eagerly cancels via the strategy on terminal events
RenderLifecycle --> FleetRegistry : strategy.cancel(provider_job_id)\non success/failure

' ============================================================
' Notes
' ============================================================

note bottom of MonitorLockSweeper
  One thread.  Per tick: iterate the four
  sweep strategies and call sweep() on each.
  Strategy exceptions are logged and skipped
  — one fleet's failure does not stall others.
end note

note bottom of VastFleetMonitor
  Per tick:
   1. SELECT active Vast rows (1 PG query)
   2. vast_client.instances.list()  (1 API call)
   3. for row: _inspect(row, fleet[row.id])
  _inspect runs the same decision blocks the
  per-job VastInstanceMonitor used to run.
end note

note bottom of ModalFleetMonitor
  Per tick:
   1. SELECT active Modal rows (1 PG query)
   2. for row: _inspect(row)
  No Modal API call per tick — the per-job
  monitor only ever read PG + Redis.  SDK
  cancel_job fires only on terminal events.
end note

note bottom of CallbackRouter
  Single funnel for fleet-monitor outcomes.
  Early-out via is_job_terminal(id) so a
  worker's mark_failed and the singleton's
  later detection collapse to one transition.
end note

note as NAMING #FFFFCC
  **"monitor_lock" is a misnomer.**
   The module's job is broader than locking — it owns:
    1. The 30s sweep daemon thread (MonitorLockSweeper)
    2. Four sweep strategies (3 fleet + 1 group audit)
    3. The Redis lock primitive (MonitorLockRepository) used
       by the fleet singletons themselves, not by this module
   Only #3 is "lock" in nature.  Rename candidates worth considering:
      sweep_daemon / fleet_supervisor / runtime_sweeper
   Holding off until structure is approved.
end note

@enduml
